description:
For a two-class and a multi-class model, shall we add `oob = scales::squish_infinite` when `prob_scaling = TRUE`? It would squish infinite values into range but still show the warning `Warning: Transformation introduced infinite values in continuous y-axis`. This warning is helpful for users to see when using logit transformation but not sure if squishing by default is the right choice. 

```
if (prob_scaling) {
      p <- p + ggplot2::scale_x_continuous(
        oob = scales::squish_infinite,
        trans = scales::logit_trans(),
        breaks = prob_breaks
      )
    }
```
